    "plotType": "Semi-log line plot (log optical density vs. time)",
    "description": "A bacterial growth curve tracks how a liquid culture's density changes over time, usually plotted with cell count or optical density on a logarithmic y-axis. Its S-shape reveals four phases: a flat lag while cells adapt, a straight exponential (log) climb where they double at a fixed rate, a plateau as nutrients run out (stationary), and a final decline as cells die. Microbiologists use it to characterize a strain's fitness, set the right harvest point, and compare how conditions or mutations change growth.",
